% Generate pdd/cloud_server/app.py as the self-hosted FastAPI service.

Export create_app(settings: ServerSettings|None = None) -> FastAPI.
Initialize SQLite during lifespan. Authenticate all contract APIs with constant-time bearer-token matching.
The configured token determines ownership; API bodies cannot select another owner.
Keep /health public. Expose validated generation, relay, and example routes from the contract.
Support exact configured CORS origins, GET/POST, Authorization, Content-Type, and Idempotency-Key.
Bound streamed request bodies before JSON parsing to max_body_bytes.
Errors use {error: message}; validation adds field/message details without echoing request contents.
Sanitize inference failures as HTTP 502, retaining diagnostics in the server log.
getCreditBalance reports billingEnabled=false and null balances.
syncState and trackUsage return authenticated HTTP 501 because their public request contracts are absent.
Serve bundled assets, logo.svg, /cloud, and /connect/{session_id}; redirect / to cloud.
Validate the connect path's session_id as 1..128 characters and expose it in OpenAPI.
Return 503 with Bun build instructions if the frontend is missing.
Never require Firebase, a PDD Cloud account, or deployment credentials.

